  "notes": "First issue with liner notes in black typeface on rear cover.\nLabel variant to [r=7702070], with different layout of \"Side 1\"/\"Side 2\" text.\nColored cardstock inner sleeve, \"PC 33235\" printed in white on lower left corner.\n\n\"T\" etched in runouts denotes [l=Columbia Records Pressing Plant, Terre Haute], pressing. Remainder of runouts mostly stamped.\n\nAll Selections (ASCAP)\n\nLyric extracts in liner notes: © 1974 Rams Horn Music\n© 1974 CBS Inc./℗ 1974 CBS Inc.\nManufactured by Columbia Records\nCBS Inc.\n\nLiner notes: New York, 1974\n\nHype sticker on some copies, with catalog number:\nFeaturing\n\"Tangled Up In Blue\"\n\"Idiot Wind\"\n\"Lily, Rosemary And The Jack Of Hearts\"",
  "released_formatted": "20 Jan 1975",
